# Result files are an append-only record log: each line is a self-contained,
# immutable measurement keyed by a globally unique `run_id`, and line order
# carries no meaning. Two branches that each append distinct records are not in
# conflict — the correct resolution is the union of both, which is what git
# cannot infer on its own and would otherwise escalate to a manual merge on
# every concurrent run.
#
# Scoped to exactly these files, deliberately. `merge=union` on structured text
# (JSON, YAML, TOML, source) silently produces syntactically broken output by
# interleaving hunks, so this must never be widened to a directory that holds
# anything but JSONL. It is safe here only because every line stands alone.
#
# Backstop: `results_are_valid` asserts `run_id` uniqueness across the whole
# tree, so if a union merge ever double-applies a line, CI says so rather than
# the duplicate being silently medianed into a published number.
results/**/*.jsonl merge=union

# Keep line endings stable for the fixtures the golden tests compare byte-wise.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.avsc  text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
